on3 -c \\\"import slug; [getattr(slug,n)() for n in dir(slug) if n.startswith(''test_'')]\\\").\\n\\nYour job is review only: do NOT edit the file. List any bugs, edge cases that give wrong or surprising output, and gaps in the tests. For each finding give a concrete input, the actual output, and what it should be, ranked by severity. If you find nothing real, say so. Keep the report concise.\\nEOF\\ndone\",\"description\":\"Start Codex and Fable review agents\",\"content\":\"FLOTILLA 6a532dfb-d90c-4b9a-9283-18d6355ae904 {\\\"op\\\":\\\"agent\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"6a532dfb-d90c-4b9a-9283-18d6355ae904\\\",\\\"agent\\\":\\\"codex\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"gpt-6.1-sol\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Review slug.py (gpt-6.1-sol)\\\",\\\"task\\\":\\\"Please review the file /home/user/slug.py. It contains a Python function slugify(title, max_length=None) that turns titles into URL slugs, plus a few test functions (pytest isn''t installed; you can run them with: cd ~ && python3 -c \\\\\\\"import slug; [getattr(slug,n)() for n in dir(slug) if n.startswith(''test_'')]\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\nYour job is review only: do NOT edit the file. List any bugs, edge cases that give wrong or surprising output, and gaps in the tests. For each finding give a concrete input, the actual output, and what it should be, ranked by severity. If you find nothing real, say so. Keep the report concise.\\\"}\\nStarted 6a532dfb-d90c-4b9a-9283-18d6355ae904 in this VM. It answers with the other agents you start this turn, in one message starting with [flotilla] once all of them have, and you get a new turn then. Start any others now; don''t wait or poll: do other work, or end your turn.\\nFLOTILLA 7d366475-2fa8-4b43-abe5-fa1aeb9759ee {\\\"op\\\":\\\"agent\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"7d366475-2fa8-4b43-abe5-fa1aeb9759ee\\\",\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude-code\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-fable-5-1\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Review slug.py (claude-fable-5-1)\\\",\\\"task\\\":\\\"Please review the file /home/user/slug.py. It contains a Python function slugify(title, max_length=None) that turns titles into URL slugs, plus a few test functions (pytest isn''t installed; you can run them with: cd ~ && python3 -c \\\\\\\"import slug; [getattr(slug,n)() for n in dir(slug) if n.startswith(''test_'')]\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\nYour job is review only: do NOT edit the file. List any bugs, edge cases that give wrong or surprising output, and gaps in the tests. For each finding give a concrete input, the actual output, and what it should be, ranked by severity. If you find nothing real, say so. Keep the report concise.\\\"}\\nStarted 7d366475-2fa8-4b43-abe5-fa1aeb9759ee in this VM. It answers with the other agents you start this turn, in one message starting with [flotilla] once all of them have, and you get a new turn then. Start any others now; don''t wait or poll: do other work, or end your turn.\",\"error\":false}","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_014LK735Y8wDSWszunuZbmLf"}}],"is_reverted":false},"conversationId":"69ef1ed3-691d-46fc-8fda-ab1917409927"}', 1, '2026-11-01T03:39:43.544Z');
INSERT INTO events (thread_id, key, event_id, task_id, type, timestamp, raw_json, settled, received_at) VALUES ('a866986f-1097-4727-8a2b-63218953dc43', 'e6a9f229-3298-4d29-bdfe-10e2a623f206', 'e6a9f229-3298-4d29-bdfe-10e2a623f206', '76147ad8-bbbc-4e31-933b-46448d44aaa6', 'response', 1793504385167, '{"id":"e6a9f229-3298-4d29-bdfe-10e2a623f206","type":"response","timestamp":1793504385167,"taskId":"76147ad8-bbbc-4e31-933b-46448d44aaa6","data":{"content":"I wrote `slugify(title, max_length=None)` and six tests in `~/slug.py`; the tests pass, run without pytest because it isn''t installed here. I''ve sent the file to Codex (gpt-6.1-sol) and to Claude Code on Fable (claude-fable-5-1) for a review-only pass; once they report I''ll fix what they find and tell you in three lines who caught what.","model":"claude-opus-5-5","is_reverted":false},"conversationId":"69ef1ed3-691d-46fc-8fda-ab1917409927"}', 1, '2026-11-01T03:39:46.576Z');
INSERT INTO events (thread_id, key, event_id, task_id, type, timestamp, raw_json, settled, received_at) VALUES ('a866986f-1097-4727-8a2b-63218953dc43', 'f1a4a457-a8ea-40bb-a852-5d0973a25e89', 'e206aa9b-15c1-423c-b2a6-dd524a5c1069', 'f1a4a457-a8ea-40bb-a852-5d0973a25e89', 'prompt', 1793504417338, '{"id":"e206aa9b-15c1-423c-b2a6-dd524a5c1069","type":"prompt","timestamp":1793504417338,"taskId":"f1a4a457-a8ea-40bb-a852-5d0973a25e89","conversationId":"69ef1ed3-691d-46fc-8fda-ab1917409927","data":{"prompt":"[flotilla] Agents answered (2):\n\n### \"Review slug.py (gpt-6.1-sol)\" (6a532dfb-d90c-4b9a-9283-18d6355ae904) finished:\n\nAll six existing tests pass. File unchanged.\n\nRanked findings:\n\n1. **Medium — Unicode separators disappear, merging words (line 13).**  \n   `slugify(\"foo—bar\")` → `\"foobar\"`; should be `\"foo-bar\"` to preserve the word boundary. ASCII punctuation becomes a separator, but Unicode punctuation is deleted first. Missing test: Unicode dashes and other Unicode separators.\n\n2. **Low — Negative maximum lengths silently slice from the end (line 18).**  \n   `slugify(\"hello world\", -1)` → `\"hello-worl\"`; should reject a negative limit with `ValueError` (or explicitly document another policy). Missing tests: negative limits, zero, and limits exceeding the slug length.\n\n3. **Low — ASCII conversion loses some letters rather than transliterating them (line 13).**  \n   `slugify(\"Straße\")` → `\"strae\"`; `\"strasse\"` would preserve the title’s meaning better. This is a transliteration limitation, not a violation of the documented ASCII-output guarantee. The accent test does not cover letters without ASCII decompositions.\n\n**Additional test gap:** truncation inside a word is unspecified: `slugify(\"hello wonderful world\", 8)` → `\"hello-wo\"`. That is valid character-based truncation; if whole-word truncation is intended, it should be `\"hello\"`. Add a test documenting the intended behavior.\n\n### \"Review slug.py (claude-fable-5-1)\" (7d366475-2fa8-4b43-abe5-fa1aeb9759ee) finished:\n\nTests pass as written. The function is sound for Latin-1 accented text, but it has real gaps around non-decomposable letters, non-Latin scripts, and `max_length`. Findings ranked by severity:\n\n**1. Letters with no NFKD decomposition are silently dropped (wrong output).** The `encode(\"ascii\", \"ignore\")` step deletes any character NFKD can''t reduce to ASCII, which mangles common European words.\n\n| Input | Actual | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Straße` | `strae` | `strasse` |\n| `Ærøskøbing` | `rskbing` | `aeroskobing` |\n| `Łódź` | `odz` | `lodz` |\n| `Tschüß` | `tschu` | `tschuss` |\n\nA transliteration table for ß, æ, ø, ł, đ, þ, œ, etc. (or a library like `text-unidecode`) is the usual fix.\n\n**2. Non-Latin titles produce an empty slug.** `日本語のタイトル` and `Привет мир` both return `''''`, the same as `\"!!!\"`. Callers get no signal that a real title was lost, which typically yields duplicate or blank URLs. Either transliterate, or document that the return value can be empty and that callers must fall back to an ID.\n\n**3. Negative `max_length` truncates from the wrong end.** `slugify(\"hello-world\", -3)` returns `''hello-wo''` because Python slicing treats negatives as \"drop from the end\". It should raise `ValueError` or be treated as no limit. `max_length=0` returns `''''`, which is arguably fine but worth a deliberate choice.\n\n**4. Apostrophes become word breaks (surprising, low severity).** `\"don''t stop\"` gives `don-t-stop` and `\"O’Neil’s\"` gives `oneils` only because the curly quote happens to be dropped by the ASCII step. Straight and curly apostrophes are handled inconsistently. Most slugifiers strip apostrophes before splitting so both give `dont-stop` / `oneils`.\n\n**5. `None` is slugified to `\"none\"`.** `str(title)` means `slugify(None)` returns `''none''` rather than raising. Probably unintended for a title field.\n\n**6. Compatibility decomposition oddities (minor, likely acceptable).** `½ cup` becomes `12-cup` and `x²+y²` becomes `x2-y2`. NFKD maps vulgar fractions and superscripts to plain digits, which loses meaning. Worth knowing, not necessarily worth fixing.\n\n**Test gaps:**\n- No test for ß / æ / ø / ł style letters, so finding 1 is invisible.\n- No test for non-Latin input, so the empty-slug behaviour is undocumented.\n- `max_length` is tested once with a case that lands exactly on a hyphen. Missing: a cut mid-word that leaves no trailing hyphen (`max_length=7` gives `hello-w`), a limit longer than the slug, 0, and negative values.\n- No test for apostrophes or curly quotes.\n- No test for non-string input (`None`, int).\n- The docstring example is not run anywhere since there''s no doctest hook; it''s fine but redundant with `test_basic`.\n\nNo crashes found for any string input. The implementation is a reasonable minimal slugifier, but the silent character loss in finding 1 is the one I''d call a bug rather than a design choice.","status":"finished","is_reverted":false}}', 1, '2026-11-01T03:40:42.066Z');
INSERT INTO events (thread_id, key, event_id, task_id, type, timestamp, raw_json, settled, received_at) VALUES ('a866986f-1097-4727-8a2b-63218953dc43', 'ccf331e7-c2b6-4f4a-89d3-a03efcc96a87', 'ccf331e7-c2b6-4f4a-89d3-a03efcc96a87', 'f1a4a457-a8ea-40bb-a852-5d0973a25e89', 'response', 1793504435071, '{"id":"ccf331e7-c2b6-4f4a-89d3-a03efcc96a87","type":"response","timestamp":1793504435071,"taskId":"f1a4a457-a8ea-40bb-a852-5d0973a25e89","data":{"content":"","model":"claude-opus-5-5","tools":[{"use":{"id":"toolu_01BZs92CPmJPh2ohR8cAcdzL","name":"Bash","type":"tool_use","input":{"command":"cd ~ && cat > slug.py <<''EOF''\n\"\"\"URL slug generation.\"\"\"\nimport re\nimport unicodedata\n\n# Letters that NFKD can''t reduce to ASCII (applied after lowercasing).\n_TRANSLIT = str.maketrans({\n    \"ß\": \"ss\", \"æ\": \"ae\", \"œ\": \"oe\", \"ø\": \"o\", \"ł\": \"l\", \"đ\": \"d\",\n    \"ð\": \"d\", \"þ\": \"th\", \"ı\": \"i\", \"ħ\": \"h\", \"ŧ\": \"t\", \"ŋ\": \"ng\",\n})\n_APOSTROPHES = re.compile(r\"[''’ʼ‘`]\")\n\n\ndef slugify(title, max_length=None):\n    \"\"\"Turn a title into a lowercase, hyphen-separated, ASCII URL slug.\n\n    Characters with no ASCII equivalent (e.g. CJK, Cyrillic) act as\n    separators, so a fully non-Latin title returns '''' -- callers should\n    fall back to an ID. max_length truncates by character, then strips\n    any trailing hyphen.\n\n    >>> slugify(\"Hello, World!\")\n    ''hello-world''\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(title, str):\n        raise TypeError(f\"title must be str, not {type(title).__name__}\")\n    if max_length is not None and max_length < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"max_length must be >= 0\")\n    text = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", title.lower()).translate(_TRANSLIT)\n    text = \"\".join(c for c in text if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n    text = _APOSTROPHES.sub(\"\", text)\n    # Anything else non-alphanumeric (incl. Unicode dashes) is a word break.\n    text = re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", text).strip(\"-\")\n    if max_length is not None:\n        text = text[:max_length].rstrip(\"-\")\n    return text\n\n\n# --- tests (run with: python -m pytest slug.py) ---\n\ndef _raises(exc, fn, *args):\n    try:\n        fn(*args)\n    except exc:\n        return True\n    return False\n\n\ndef test_basic():\n    assert slugify(\"Hello, World!\") == \"hello-world\"\n\n\ndef test_accents():\n    assert slugify(\"Crème Brûlée à la Mode\") == \"creme-brulee-a-la-mode\"\n\n\ndef test_non_decomposable_letters():\n    assert slugify(\"Straße\") == \"strasse\"\n    assert slugify(\"Ærøskøbing\") == \"aeroskobing\"\n    assert slugify(\"Łódź\") == \"lodz\"\n    assert slugify(\"Tschüß\") == \"tschuss\"\n\n\ndef test_unicode_separators_keep_word_breaks():\n    assert slugify(\"foo—bar\") == \"foo-bar\"\n    assert slugify(\"foo–bar…baz\") == \"foo-bar-baz\"\n\n\ndef test_apostrophes():\n    assert slugify(\"don''t stop\") == \"dont-stop\"\n    assert slugify(\"O’Neil’s\") == \"oneils\"\n\n\ndef test_non_latin_is_empty():\n    assert slugify(\"日本語のタイトル\") == \"\"\n    assert slugify(\"Привет мир\") == \"\"\n    assert slugify(\"Привет world\") == \"world\"\n\n\ndef test_collapses_and_strips_separators():\n    assert slugify(\"  --Foo   &&  Bar__ \") == \"foo-bar\"\n\n\ndef test_numbers():\n    assert slugify(\"Top 10 Tips for 2026\") == \"top-10-tips-for-2026\"\n\n\ndef test_empty_and_symbols_only():\n    assert slugify(\"\") == \"\"\n    assert slugify(\"!!!\") == \"\"\n\n\ndef test_max_length():\n    assert slugify(\"hello wonderful world\", max_length=6) == \"hello\"\n    assert slugify(\"hello wonderful world\", max_length=8) == \"hello-wo\"\n    assert slugify(\"hello\", max_length=50) == \"hello\"\n    assert slugify(\"hello\", max_length=0) == \"\"\n    assert _raises(ValueError, slugify, \"hello world\", -1)\n\n\ndef test_non_string_rejected():\n    assert _raises(TypeError, slugify, None)\n    assert _raises(TypeError, slugify, 42)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import slug; ts=[n for n in dir(slug) if n.startswith(''test_'')]; [getattr(slug,n)() for n in ts]; print(len(ts),''passed'')\" && python3 -m doctest slug.py && echo doctest ok","description":"Apply review fixes and rerun tests"}},"result":{"type":"tool_result","content":"{\"type\":\"bash_output\",\"pending\":false,\"command\":\"cd ~ && cat > slug.py <<''EOF''\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"URL slug generation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport re\\nimport unicodedata\\n\\n# Letters that NFKD can''t reduce to ASCII (applied after lowercasing).\\n_TRANSLIT = str.maketrans({\\n    \\\"ß\\\": \\\"ss\\\", \\\"æ\\\": \\\"ae\\\", \\\"œ\\\": \\\"oe\\\", \\\"ø\\\": \\\"o\\\", \\\"ł\\\": \\\"l\\\", \\\"đ\\\": \\\"d\\\",\\n    \\\"ð\\\": \\\"d\\\", \\\"þ\\\": \\\"th\\\", \\\"ı\\\": \\\"i\\\", \\\"ħ\\\": \\\"h\\\", \\\"ŧ\\\": \\\"t\\\", \\\"ŋ\\\": \\\"ng\\\",\\n})\\n_APOSTROPHES = re.compile(r\\\"[''’ʼ‘`]\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef slugify(title, max_length=None):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Turn a title into a lowercase, hyphen-separated, ASCII URL slug.\\n\\n    Characters with no ASCII equivalent (e.g. CJK, Cyrillic) act as\\n    separators, so a fully non-Latin title returns '''' -- callers should\\n    fall back to an ID. max_length truncates by character, then strips\\n    any trailing hyphen.\\n\\n    >>> slugify(\\\"Hello, World!\\\")\\n    ''hello-world''\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not isinstance(title, str):\\n        raise TypeError(f\\\"title must be str, not {type(title).__name__}\\\")\\n    if max_length is not None and max_length < 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"max_length must be >= 0\\\")\\n    text = unicodedata.normalize(\\\"NFKD\\\", title.lower()).translate(_TRANSLIT)\\n    text = \\\"\\\".join(c for c in text if not unicodedata.combining(c))\\n    text = _APOSTROPHES.sub(\\\"\\\", text)\\n    # Anything else non-alphanumeric (incl. Unicode dashes) is a word break.\\n    text = re.sub(r\\\"[^a-z0-9]+\\\", \\\"-\\\", text).strip(\\\"-\\\")\\n    if max_length is not None:\\n        text = text[:max_length].rstrip(\\\"-\\\")\\n    return text\\n\\n\\n# --- tests (run with: python -m pytest slug.py) ---\\n\\ndef _raises(exc, fn, *args):\\n    try:\\n        fn(*args)\\n    except exc:\\n        return True\\n    return False\\n\\n\\ndef test_basic():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"Hello, World!\\\") == \\\"hello-world\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_accents():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"Crème Brûlée à la Mode\\\") == \\\"creme-brulee-a-la-mode\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_non_decomposable_letters():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"Straße\\\") == \\\"strasse\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"Ærøskøbing\\\") == \\\"aeroskobing\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"Łódź\\\") == \\\"lodz\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"Tschüß\\\") == \\\"tschuss\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_unicode_separators_keep_word_breaks():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"foo—bar\\\") == \\\"foo-bar\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"foo–bar…baz\\\") == \\\"foo-bar-baz\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_apostrophes():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"don''t stop\\\") == \\\"dont-stop\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"O’Neil’s\\\") == \\\"oneils\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_non_latin_is_empty():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"日本語のタイトル\\\") == \\\"\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"Привет мир\\\") == \\\"\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"Привет world\\\") == \\\"world\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_collapses_and_strips_separators():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"  --Foo   &&  Bar__ \\\") == \\\"foo-bar\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_numbers():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"Top 10 Tips for 2026\\\") == \\\"top-10-tips-for-2026\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_empty_and_symbols_only():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"\\\") == \\\"\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"!!!\\\") == \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_max_length():\\n    assert slugify(\\\"hello wonderful world\\\", max_length=6) == \\\"hello\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"hello wonderful world\\\", max_length=8) == \\\"hello-wo\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"hello\\\", max_length=50) == \\\"hello\\\"\\n    assert slugify(\\\"hello\\\", max_length=0) == \\\"\\\"\\n    assert _raises(ValueError, slugify, \\\"hello world\\\", -1)\\n\\n\\ndef test_non_string_rejected():\\n    assert _raises(TypeError, slugify, None)\\n    assert _raises(TypeError, slugify, 42)\\nEOF\\npython3 -c \\\"import slug; ts=[n for n in dir(slug) if n.startswith(''test_'')]; [getattr(slug,n)() for n in ts]; print(len(ts),''passed'')\\\" && python3 -m doctest slug.py && echo doctest ok\",\"description\":\"Apply review fixes and rerun tests\",\"content\":\"11 passed\\ndoctest ok\",\"error\":false}","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BZs92CPmJPh2ohR8cAcdzL"}}],"is_reverted":false},"conversationId":"69ef1ed3-691d-46fc-8fda-ab1917409927"}', 1, '2026-11-01T03:40:35.997Z');
INSERT INTO events (thread_id, key, event_id, task_id, type, timestamp, raw_json, settled, received_at) VALUES ('a866986f-1097-4727-8a2b-63218953dc43', '6ea35c1a-43b8-4eaa-bcb1-a66903e841f1', '6ea35c1a-43b8-4eaa-bcb1-a66903e841f1', 'f1a4a457-a8ea-40bb-a852-5d0973a25e89', 'response', 1793504440593, '{"id":"6ea35c1a-43b8-4eaa-bcb1-a66903e841f1","type":"response","timestamp":1793504440593,"taskId":"f1a4a457-a8ea-40bb-a852-5d0973a25e89","data":{"content":"- **Both caught:** letters like ß, æ, ø and ł were being dropped (`Straße` gave `strae`), and a negative `max_length` cut characters off the end instead of failing. Both are fixed: those letters now convert to ASCII equivalents (`strasse`), and a negative limit raises `ValueError`.\n- **Only Codex caught:** Unicode dashes were deleted, which merged words (`foo—bar` gave `foobar`); they now act as separators. It also asked for tests that pin down the mid-word cut (`hello-wo`), so I kept cutting by character, documented it, and added those tests.\n- **Only Fable caught:** non-Latin titles silently return `''''` (now documented, with a note that callers should fall back to an ID), `don''t` gave `don-t` (apostrophes are now removed), and `slugify(None)` returned `''none''` (non-strings now raise `TypeError`). I left `½` turning into `12` as Fable suggested; the 11 tests and the doctest in `~/slug.py` all pass.","model":"claude-opus-5-5","is_reverted":false},"conversationId":"69ef1ed3-691d-46fc-8fda-ab1917409927"}', 1, '2026-11-01T03:40:42.066Z');
