INSERT INTO kv (key, value, updated_at) VALUES ('side:fc759ff4-7108-4936-abc3-c4bbe2bc20e4:b4558cd4-6442-42bc-ba02-a29098b2720c', '{"id":"b4558cd4-6442-42bc-ba02-a29098b2720c","title":"Review slugify (Codex)","provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","task":"Please review the Python file /home/user/slug.py. It defines slugify(title, max_length=80), which turns a title into a URL slug, plus a few tests (run them with `python3 /home/user/slug.py`; pytest isn''t installed).\n\nDo NOT edit the file. Just review it and list any bugs you find: wrong output, edge cases it gets wrong, crashes, or tests that are wrong or missing for important cases. For each bug give a concrete input, what it returns now, and what it should return. Order them most serious first. If you find no real bugs, say so; don''t pad the list with style nits.","batch":"4d658f26-c82c-43c9-af03-a61805611625","conversation":"fee73d5d-c493-4f39-8860-46fe33042122","status":"finished","error":null,"calls":2,"latest":null,"answer":"1. **Non-ASCII dash punctuation merges words.**  \n   Input: `slugify(\"red‑blue\")` (non-breaking hyphen)  \n   Returns now: `\"redblue\"`  \n   Should return: `\"red-blue\"`  \n   Non-ASCII punctuation is discarded during ASCII encoding before the non-alphanumeric-to-hyphen substitution. The same affects `slugify(\"foo—bar\")`, which returns `\"foobar\"` instead of `\"foo-bar\"`. This contradicts the intended hyphen-separated output and the comment that non-alphanumeric runs become hyphens. A Unicode-dash test is missing.\n\n2. **Negative `max_length` silently produces an invalid-length slug.**  \n   Input: `slugify(\"hello-world\", max_length=-1)`  \n   Returns now: `\"hello\"`  \n   Should: raise `ValueError` (a negative maximum length is invalid).  \n   The result cannot satisfy the requested maximum (`len(\"hello\") > -1`). Negative-length validation and a corresponding test are missing.","started_ms":1793498379438,"ended_ms":1793498462783,"reported":true}', '2026-11-01T02:01:03.037Z');
INSERT INTO kv (key, value, updated_at) VALUES ('side:fc759ff4-7108-4936-abc3-c4bbe2bc20e4:2e1fb20f-7afd-42d7-a21d-c7bf74ce445f', '{"id":"2e1fb20f-7afd-42d7-a21d-c7bf74ce445f","title":"Review slugify (Haiku)","provider":"claude-code","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","task":"Please review the Python file /home/user/slug.py. It defines slugify(title, max_length=80), which turns a title into a URL slug, plus a few tests (run them with `python3 /home/user/slug.py`; pytest isn''t installed).\n\nDo NOT edit the file. Just review it and list any bugs you find: wrong output, edge cases it gets wrong, crashes, or tests that are wrong or missing for important cases. For each bug give a concrete input, what it returns now, and what it should return. Order them most serious first. If you find no real bugs, say so; don''t pad the list with style nits.","batch":"4d658f26-c82c-43c9-af03-a61805611625","conversation":"36576178-04b7-42ad-bc14-69f2170bd30c","status":"finished","error":null,"calls":2,"latest":null,"answer":"I did not edit the file. `python3 /home/user/slug.py` prints \"7 tests passed\", but the tests miss the bugs below. I confirmed each output by running it.\n\n1. **Letters with no Unicode decomposition are deleted, so words are corrupted.** Line 16 (`encode(\"ascii\", \"ignore\")`) drops them outright. Actual vs. expected:\n   - `\"Straße\"` → `\"strae\"`, should be `\"strasse\"`\n   - `\"Søren Kierkegaard\"` → `\"sren-kierkegaard\"`, should be `\"soren-kierkegaard\"`\n   - `\"Łódź\"` → `\"odz\"`, should be `\"lodz\"`\n   - `\"Æsop\"` → `\"sop\"`, should be `\"aesop\"`\n   - `\"Œuvre\"` → `\"uvre\"`, should be `\"oeuvre\"`\n   - `\"Đà Nẵng\"` → `\"a-nang\"`, should be `\"da-nang\"`\n\n2. **Em dashes, en dashes, emoji and CJK between words join the words.** The same ASCII-ignore step removes them without inserting a separator, so the surrounding words run together.\n   - `\"Tokyo—Paris\"` (em dash) → `\"tokyoparis\"`, should be `\"tokyo-paris\"`\n   - `\"Tokyo–Paris\"` (en dash) → `\"tokyoparis\"`, should be `\"tokyo-paris\"`\n   - `\"Pizza🍕Night\"` → `\"pizzanight\"`, should be `\"pizza-night\"`\n   - `\"Hello世界World\"` → `\"helloworld\"`, should be `\"hello-world\"`\n\n   Fixing this needs apostrophes (which should be deleted) handled separately from other non-ASCII characters (which should become separators). The current code does not distinguish them.\n\n3. **Negative `max_length` slices from the end.** `slugify(\"hello world\", max_length=-3)` → `\"hello\"`. The `len(text) > max_length` check is always true, and `text[:-3]` cuts off the tail. It should raise `ValueError`. Separately, `max_length=0` silently returns `\"\"`; that is arguably fine, but nothing pins it down.\n\n4. **Non-Latin-only titles return an empty string.** `slugify(\"北京\")` → `\"\"`. The function has no fallback, so a caller can get an empty slug with no error. Whether that is acceptable is a design decision; I''d flag it rather than call it a bug.\n\n5. **Dead code (not an output bug).** The `[''’]` in line 19 never matches a curly apostrophe, because line 16 already removed it. `\"Don’t\"` → `\"dont\"` only works by way of line 16. `test_apostrophes` passes, so it does not show the regex is redundant.\n\n**Missing or wrong tests:**\n- Nothing covers bugs 1–3. The accent test only uses decomposable characters, so it can''t catch them.\n- No test for a dash or emoji between words (bug 2).\n- No test for an exact-fit truncation, e.g. `slugify(\"one two three\", 7)` → `\"one-two\"`.\n- No test pinning the behaviour when one word is longer than `max_length`. `slugify(\"supercalifragilistic\", 10)` → `\"supercalif\"`, a mid-word cut. This may be intended, but it should be a test either way.\n- No test for `max_length` ≤ 0 or for `TypeError` on non-str input.\n- The module comment says `python -m pytest slug.py`, but pytest isn''t installed. The `__main__` runner is the one that works. Also, the docstring doctest is never run.","started_ms":1793498379616,"ended_ms":1793498423713,"reported":true}', '2026-11-01T02:01:03.037Z');
INSERT INTO kv (key, value, updated_at) VALUES ('mentions:fc759ff4-7108-4936-abc3-c4bbe2bc20e4', '{"entries":[{"kind":"skill","name":"boat","description":"Use sandboxes from inside a sandbox. Covers sandbox/boat-dev lifecycle, self/current aliases, SSH, desktop, prompts, event reading, file copy, port forwarding, hosted services, QA, scraping, desktop/browser work, and small multi-Sandbox orchestration.","harness":"claude-code","insert":"/boat","shadowed":false},{"kind":"skill","name":"sandbox","description":"Use sandboxes from inside a sandbox. Covers sandbox/boat-dev lifecycle, self/current aliases, SSH, desktop, prompts, event reading, file copy, port forwarding, hosted services, QA, scraping, desktop/browser work, and small multi-Sandbox orchestration.","harness":"codex","insert":"$sandbox","shadowed":false},{"kind":"skill","name":"imagegen","description":"Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas.","harness":"codex","insert":"$imagegen","shadowed":false},{"kind":"skill","name":"openai-docs","description":"Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and self-knowledge—including ''you,'' ''your,'' ''this app,'' or ''this coding agent'' when they refer to Codex—and for OpenAI APIs/products and ChatGPT Work. Also use for model choice/migration, prompting, SDKs, Responses, Realtime, agents, evals, and Chat/Work/Codex comparisons. Do not use for generic app/software tasks that merely mention Codex.","harness":"codex","insert":"$openai-docs","shadowed":false},{"kind":"skill","name":"review-agent","description":"Perform a read-only, defect-first review of a specified code change and return every actionable finding. Use when another agent delegates review of uncommitted changes, a base-branch diff, a commit, or custom review instructions.","harness":"codex","insert":"$review-agent","shadowed":false},{"kind":"skill","name":"skill-creator","description":"Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources.","harness":"codex","insert":"$skill-creator","shadowed":false},{"kind":"skill","name":"skill-installer","description":"Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo (including private repos).","harness":"codex","insert":"$skill-installer","shadowed":false},{"kind":"skill","name":"sandbox","description":"Use sandboxes from inside a sandbox. Covers sandbox/boat-dev lifecycle, self/current aliases, SSH, desktop, prompts, event reading, file copy, port forwarding, hosted services, QA, scraping, desktop/browser work, and small multi-Sandbox orchestration.","harness":"opencode","insert":"/sandbox","shadowed":false},{"kind":"skill","name":"sandbox","description":"Use sandboxes from inside a sandbox. Covers sandbox/boat-dev lifecycle, self/current aliases, SSH, desktop, prompts, event reading, file copy, port forwarding, hosted services, QA, scraping, desktop/browser work, and small multi-Sandbox orchestration.","harness":"opencode","insert":"/sandbox","shadowed":true},{"kind":"command","name":"compact","description":"Summarise the conversation to free context","harness":"claude-code","insert":"/compact","shadowed":false},{"kind":"command","name":"init","description":"Create or update AGENTS.md for this project","harness":"opencode","insert":"/in